<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44494" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sīthŏnĭi</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σιθόνιοι</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Thracian people;</i> hence, <b>poet.</b>, in gen., <i>the
			Thracians</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 11, 18, § 41</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Hor. C.
				1, 18</span></i>. 9.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sīthŏnĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>Sithonian</i>, <i>Thracian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 13, 571</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nives,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 10, 66</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3, 26, 10</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aquilo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					11, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nurus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					6, 588</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					P. 4, 7, 25</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sīthon</span></b> ,
				ŏnis, adj., <i>Sithonian</i>, <i>Thracian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sithones et Scythici triumphi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					3, 719</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sī-thŏnis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, <i>adj. f.</i>,
				<i>Sithonian</i>, <i>Thracian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">unda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					2, 6</span></i>
			.—Subst., <i>a Thracian
				woman</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. R. Am.
		605</span></i>.</div>
